            <div type="translation" source="bib:Kuppusamy+al2010_01">
                <p n="1">Hail! Prosperity!</p>
                <p n="1-2">3rd year <supplied reason="subaudible">of the reign</supplied> of the king Parakēsaripanmar who took
the head of Vīrapāṇṭiyaṉ.</p>
                <p n="2-10">The never dying and never aging sheep donated by Kaliyaṉ Maṉṟāṭi Aiyyaṉ alias Ācārakānta-p-pallavaraiyaṉ, a share holder <supplied reason="explanation"><foreign>karai uṭaiyāṉ</foreign></supplied> of Netimūr-nāṭu in Cempūr-k-kōṭṭam <supplied reason="explanation">an administrative division</supplied>, for a perpetual lamp to the great Lord of śrī-Mūlastāṉam of Vākūr, are
ninety-six; the standing lamp set up to burn is one.</p>
                <p n="10-11">These are under the protection of the great Śaiva devotees.</p>
            </div>
            
